{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 39,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David. I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from good; and my sorrow was stirred.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I spoke with my tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, make me to know my end, and the measure of my days, what it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I may know how frail I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou hast made my days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hand-breadth; and my age ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " altogether vanity. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely every man walketh in a vain show: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "riches",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and knoweth not who shall gather them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now, LORD, what wait I for? my hope ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remove thy stroke away from me; I am consumed by the blow of thy hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear to my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a stranger with thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a sojourner, as all my fathers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.39.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.39.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
